#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
build-icon.py — assemble an openable .icon bundle from an extracted.json
produced by icon-extract.

Usage:
    build-icon.py <extract-dir> <output.icon> [raw-svg-dir]

<extract-dir> is the directory icon-extract wrote (containing extracted.json
plus the per-layer .svg/.png assets). It reconstructs icon.json with the
layer/group hierarchy, blend modes, opacity, translucency, specular, shadow,
blur and per-appearance fill specializations, and copies the layer assets into
<output.icon>/Assets/. When raw-svg-dir is supplied, original SVG rendition
bytes from the minimal extraction pass replace CoreSVG-generated fallbacks
before the bundle is assembled.

Set DECANT_FORMAT=26 or DECANT_FORMAT=27 to override automatic Icon Composer
schema detection for an unusually simple icon with no version-specific effects.

A reconstruction-report.json is written beside extracted.json. Set
DECANT_STRICT=1 to return a failure status whenever CoreUI exposes active
metadata that cannot be represented confidently in the selected .icon schema.
